{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire","id":385204,"title":"Dark Eras: Ruins of Empire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-29T09:56:15-08:00","id":385204,"title":"Dark Eras: Ruins of Empire","content":"So the <b>Dark Eras</b> Kickstarter is up, and you can read <i>Ruins of Empire</i>, the chapter for <b>Mummy: the Curse</b>!<br /> <br /> CAS has said he has a couple additional Eras he has in mind, including hints of a more futuristic one. Let's see what we can do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:03:24-08:00","id":385293,"title":"","content":"Just finnished it. Really digged the new Merits. Also liked the Su-Menet a lot in this Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:06:00-08:00","id":385297,"title":"","content":"For a second Mummy era, I would love to see something about the Mongol Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:37:09-08:00","id":385328,"title":"","content":"Personally, I really like the merits on offer in this new book. Makes for a more &quot;fluid&quot; schedule of awakening for the Arisen. <br /> <br /> Particularly like Interstitial Lives for broadening the &quot;Mummy without a cult&quot; idea to be a little more viable for a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:44:21-08:00","id":385350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire?p=385328#post385328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I really like the merits on offer in this new book. Makes for a more &quot;fluid&quot; schedule of awakening for the Arisen.<br /> <br /> Particularly like Interstitial Lives for broadening the &quot;Mummy without a cult&quot; idea to be a little more viable for a PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Interstitial Lives because you can chalk the awakening as the direct will of the Judges, something I found really missing in the corebook and hope 2e corrects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T12:15:51-08:00","id":385446,"title":"","content":"Hold up. Sovereign Breath. Why on earth do Mummies need to <i>breathe</i>? As the core book says under the &quot;Undeath&quot; rule, &quot;their biological metabolism only functions to the extent they choose for it&quot;. I'm pretty sure a Mummy suffering any form toxin (barring those of a magical nature) is something that only happens with the express consent of the Mummy in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T17:35:05-08:00","id":385674,"title":"","content":"Not all gases kill solely by respiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2716-jesse-heinig","name":"Jesse Heinig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2716_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:08:39-08:00","id":385685,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine many can kill something without a functioning metabolism though...<br /> <br /> And, well, the Affinity specifies &quot;Any inhaled gas&quot;. Gases that don't kill by respiration feel a bit irrelevant when it comes to discussing this Affinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:41:32-08:00","id":385692,"title":"","content":"It seems like the Undeath aspect was overlooked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T18:56:16-08:00","id":385702,"title":"","content":"Pah, no mention of the Deceived? My only grievance with an awesome setting. I'm especially in love with the new Merits and Enticement Sybaris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T01:46:33-08:00","id":386075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire?p=385702#post385702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pah, no mention of the Deceived? My only grievance with an awesome setting. I'm especially in love with the new Merits and Enticement Sybaris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe with added word count as a stretch goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:39:27-08:00","id":386206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire?p=385702#post385702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm especially in love with the new Merits and Enticement Sybaris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enticement Sybaris is pretty awesome yeah. Hopefully Mummy 2E will have some sorta &quot;Predators Aura&quot; rules with Sybaris that will allow a Mummy to use Terror, Unease or Enticement types. <br /> <br /> If I was to run Mummy again I would pretty much give every Mummy the Enticement ability. <br /> <br /> Deceived content would be nice. Possibly as another time period stretch goal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:14:03-08:00","id":386372,"title":"","content":"I find it slightly amusing that two of the new merits - Arisen Arising for no reason they know and understand, possibly because the Judges brought them back; and Judges being a little more active; are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/76194-mummy-reworked-society-creed-judges-decrees\">things I proposed a long while ago</a>. It's encouraging to see that the writers have had similar (although, obviously, more refined) ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 01-30-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:15:12-08:00","id":386373,"title":"","content":"All in all, this is a fantastic chapter that I believe captures the *feel* of this particular piece of history very well. I will definitely find some use for it in my next Mummy game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:27:27-08:00","id":386380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire?p=386372#post386372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it slightly amusing that two of the new merits - Arisen Arising for no reason they don't know and understand, possibly because the Judges brought them back; and Judges being a little more active; are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/76194-mummy-reworked-society-creed-judges-decrees\">things I proposed a long while ago</a>. It's encouraging to see that the writers have had similar (although, obviously, more refined) ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and Enticiment Sybaris will be in my list of suggestions for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T15:49:22-08:00","id":386758,"title":"","content":"I'm cool with there being merits to distinguish that your Mummy in particular might wake up for unusual reasons, but I like the baseline trio of Sothic / Cult / Tomb awakenings. It's alright, for me, that <i>sometimes </i>the Judges awaken a <i>specific</i> Mummy but I like that the other 95% of the time the Judges are distant and only interact through Descent rolls.<br /> <br /> After all, that's what sells the Deceived condition all the more as a counterpoint: the Arisen have it bad because their masters are distant and largely uncaring but the Deceived have it bad because their masters <i>are in their heads</i> and hold grudges like it's their job","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T16:31:17-08:00","id":386804,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Reseru on that point. I would like more discussion on the import of Cult Awakenings, because the fact that the Judges impose divine punishment on a Mummy avoiding a mission their <i>cult</i> gave them always seemed to rest on the roundabout justification of &quot;Mummy tells Cult when to awaken them and for what purpose, said purpose aligns with Judge's purpose, when Cult awakens Mummy it must be to further the Judge's interests&quot;. Nothing strictly seems to prevent a cult raising a Mummy with the purpose of achieving Apotheosis, and it makes the subsequent punishment by a Judge for failing to pursue that rather puzzling.<br /> <br /> But that said, the Judges are remote and distant enough for it to be justified under the old &quot;mysterious ways&quot; argument. The Mummies are just pieces on a board to the Judges, after all, and perhaps risking one could provide greater gain if it tricks an enemy, such as the Heretic, into exposing themselves...<br /> <br /> And as Reseru mentions, the very fact that all interaction with the Judges seems to happen at a third remove plays directly into reinforcing the plight of the Deceived, with their far more personal demons.<br /> <br /> It would also, you know, be nice to discuss the content of a book without bringing up a purely theoretical second edition that is, almost certainly, not going to materialise until 2017 at the earliest. The new mechanics have some interesting ramifications for the Mummy setting right at this very moment. Select Mummies who arise for no apparent reason with divine visions of their Judges' personal wishes is a pretty significant addition to the current Mummy milieu, and their apparent scarcity makes them interesting in their uniqueness as opposed to a blueprint all Mummies should follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T02:45:01-08:00","id":387181,"title":"","content":"Visions of Dead Gods is cool as a focus for a character I think, but its necessarily something that needs to be rare/unique to a small set of Mummy's to make it really work.<br /> <br /> Which I think is why I like Interstitial Lives a little better (though I like both). As you get extra wiggle room around the Sothic Turns and if your willing to sacrifice a Dot of Willpower pretty much wake up when you want as long as the ST is cool with it. <br /> <br /> I guess what I really like about the Merit is kinda removing the &quot;mandatory cult&quot; element from the game. I like Cult's but I think the option of having a Cult is more interesting then every Arisen always having one or making a new one or scrapping and old one to start again (like some weird occult matirx-manegment mini-game) . I like the idea of a Mummy who is a more of a lone figure (or maybe just has a Sadikh) who wakes up on his own under odd circumstances...basically always shows up for an adventure or lives in interesting times (I think I just described the Doctor as a Mummy...hmmm).<br /> <br /> Certainly, I could see the Heretic having this merit even before Apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T04:04:42-08:00","id":387208,"title":"","content":"In my head-canon the Heretic happened to achieve Apotheosis during this Dark Era, even if <b>Book of the Deceived</b> hints at other things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T13:28:34-08:00","id":391791,"title":"","content":"Important typo in Intersitial Lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you succeed, the effort to refill your Sheut with Sekhem costs you a Willpower dot. </div> </div> </div>Should probably say sahu, not Sheut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:08:08-08:00","id":391835,"title":"","content":"Sahu isn't really a numerical game stat. Also, forcing yourself to awaken without external purpose making it difficult to refill your Sheut Pillar kinda makes sense since that Pillar is one that's sort of metaphysically tied to Duat. Or something. In a way, anyway...in a vague, magical way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:36:22-08:00","id":391865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/385204-dark-eras-ruins-of-empire?p=391835#post391835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sahu isn't really a numerical game stat. Also, forcing yourself to awaken without external purpose making it difficult to refill your Sheut Pillar kinda makes sense since that Pillar is one that's sort of metaphysically tied to Duat. Or something. In a way, anyway...in a vague, magical way</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything else ever mentions filling Pillars with Sekhem. Pillars are kinda filled with themselves. Dragging your withered corpse back to life and filling it with the Sekhem that animates seems like the more likely reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:00:08-08:00","id":411061,"title":"","content":"So now we have a <b>Mummy</b> stretch goal teaming it up with <b>Mage</b> in the French Revolution. It's a very nice fit! Maybe I'll come back to the Kickstarter after all!<br /> <br /> (<span style=\"font-size:10px\">not that I ever wanted to give up Neolithic <b>Mage</b></span>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:56:52-08:00","id":411347,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I want Mage/Mummy French Revolution <i>so bad</i>. Doesn't help that I'm in the middle of my first time through <i>Assassin's Creed: Unity</i>, which is a franchise that I've always thought would be a good thematic fit for Mage. Add in my favorite gameline and it's practically a no-brainer for me.<